---
args: { book: ObligationBook, outcome: InvoiceOutcome }
returns: BillingOutcomeReview
---
Bind duplicate = the existing consumption entries with this exact operationId and packetId. An identical receipt and amount set is a no-op; conflicting reuse remains pending reconciliation and cannot replace earlier evidence. Bind discrepancies = verifyInvoiceOutcome(book, outcome). A nonempty discrepancy list, unknown outcome, or missing authoritative void receipt leaves consumption unchanged.

Initialize nextConsumption = book.consumption, changedConsumptionIds: string[] = [], pendingReconciliation: string[] = discrepancies. If the exact outcome is issued, match each supplied amount to the same approved packet, milestone and phase. Append one issued BillingUse per exact operation/phase with invoiceId and actual evidence receipt IDs; never increase consumption beyond its approved remaining capacity. If the exact outcome is voided and the invoice ledger confirms that operation's void at the supplied ledger version, change only those matching issued BillingUse records to void-confirmed and release only their consumed amounts. An unknown result or local void request cannot release capacity.

Bind nextBook: ObligationBook = { revision: advance only when a new authoritative outcome or matching consumption transition is established; otherwise preserve book.revision, clocks: book.clocks, acceptance: book.acceptance, earnedSlices: book.earnedSlices unchanged, consumption: nextConsumption, historicalSourceVersions: book.historicalSourceVersions plus new outcome evidence versions once }. Bind customerExplanation to the exact milestone/phase outcomes, unchanged or released capacity, and remaining evidence needed; do not recalculate earned entitlement. Return { book: nextBook, changedConsumptionIds, pendingReconciliation, customerExplanation } as BillingOutcomeReview. A repeated identical receipt is a no-op; conflicting or unknown status remains unresolved.
